<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes:   1.The above results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and are approved by the BOD of the Company at their meeting held on 23/07/2021 and have been subjected to limited review by the statutory auditors of the Company.   2.The above financial results have been prepared in accordance with the Indian Accounting Standards ( Ind AS ) as prescribed under sec 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 read with Companies (Ind AS) Rules as amended from time to time.   3.In pursuance of Sec 115BAA of the IT Act, 1961 announced by the GOI through Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 2019, the Company has an irrevocable option of shifting to lower tax rate and simultaneously forgo certain tax incentives including loss of accumulated MAT credit. The Company has not exercised this option in the current year due to unutilised MAT credit.   4.The Company has considered the possible effects that may result from COVID-19 and subsequent 2nd wave on the carrying amounts of investments. COVID-19 pandemic and subsequent 2nd wave has impacted the Textile Trading business of the company. After making internal assessments, management does not expect any significant  impact on carrying amount of its assets, including property, plant and equipment, Debtors, loans and advances, investment in subsidiaries. Management is confident of continuing as a going concern and meeting its liabilities as and when become due.       5.The Company had in earlier year given unsecured loan and business advances to its subsidiary Standard Salt Works Limited (SSWL) amounting to Rs.5969.82 lakhs(including accrued interest), which was converted into equity shares. The net worth of SSWL post such conversion had become positive and continued to remain as such during the period.   Further, in view of the long-term strategic nature of the investment in leasehold rights to salt pans and the growth prospects of the subsidiary which is engaged in the manufacture of salt from the significant leased salt pans that it is holding, no provision for diminution in the value of the investment is considered necessary at this stage.   6.The BOD have accorded their approval to enter into MOU dated 22nd March,2021 with Support Properties Pvt Ltd, Carin Properties Pvt Ltd and Feat Properties Pvt Ltd (collectively called as  Assignees ) to transfer and assign all its leasehold rights in 62.25 acres of the Company's leasehold property situated at Plot No.4, TTC Industrial Area in the villages of Ghansoli &amp; Savali, Taluka Thane ( Property''), for an overall consideration of Rs. 427.33 crores.                                                                                                                                                                                         Consequent to withdrawal of Carin Properties Pvt Ltd and Feat Properties Pvt Ltd from the above transaction  contemplated vide MOU dt 22/03/2021 viz, assignment of Leasehold rights of 62.25 acres of Company’s Leasehold property situated at Thane, only Support Properties Pvt Ltd, a party to MOU will be the Assignee.   Accordingly, BOD vide Circular Resolution dt. 03/06/2021 have given their consent to enter into a Supplemental MOU and other documents to be executed with Support Properties Pvt Ltd, at  the same overall consideration of Rs.427.33 Crores subject to various conditions precedent getting satisfied.   7.The Company has created an e-mail ID viz.,standardgrievances@rediffmail.com exclusively for the purpose of registering complaints by investors.   8.The figures for the previous quarter ended 31/03/2021 are the balancing figures between the audited figures of full financial year and the year to date figures upto  the third quarter ended 31/12/2020 which were subjected to a limited review.     9.Corresponding figures for the previous year/period have been regrouped/rearranged wherever necessary.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
